PROPOSAL: product-direction decision for the maintainer; do not implement without a go-ahead.

Evidence: a body containing "# Hijack" re-parents the following section ("Intro#Beta" becomes "Hijack#Beta", the old path answers "Heading not found"); an unclosed ``` fence swallows every later section (TOC drops from 3 entries to 1). The result is success either way. Adding a deeper heading inside a body is today the only way to create a subsection.
Options: (a) reject content with a heading at or above the section's level, and unbalanced fences; (b) accept but return the changed/new heading_paths (additive result); (c) document only.
Recommendation: (a), keeping deeper headings allowed; if an add_section tool (missing-operations card) lands first, reject all headings.

